          "reason": "K2_C0001 has an interpretable transcriptomic phenotype (oxidative phosphorylation up, NES 2.29, q=0.001, with multiple FDR-surviving programs), but this identity does not establish subtype independence. The exact-set boundary against its only neighbor K2_C0002 is weak and conflicting: native geometries show only faint within- versus between-label distinction (CT silhouette 0.013 with 0.437 negative fraction, RNA 0.079, WSI 0.050, WXS 0.091), and the pair structural screen reports a represented-but-imperfect boundary with high normalized-cut cost (0.7733) and a single-cluster-dominated union (candidate_k=1, leading eigengap 0.6977 vs 0.1440 at k=2), which is merge-compatible rather than boundary-preserving. Membership is additionally confounded: tissue source site (V=0.434, q=0.009), CT phase (V=0.316, q=0.028), CT scanner model (V=0.310, q=0.028), CT slice thickness (epsilon-squared=0.066, q=0.026), and CT z-spacing (epsilon-squared=0.048, q=0.028) remain plausible technical explanations for the observed membership. Internal subdivision is unsupported (single-cluster-dominated geometry, weak and inconsistent k>=2 solutions). With merge-compatible boundary evidence that cannot be acted on due to workflow constraints, no supported split, and no remaining evidence that could establish independence, K2_C0001 lacks defensible discovery value as an independent unit."
